# os-test (Sortix) — basic suite

Vendored from https://gitlab.com/sortix/os-test (`basic/` + `misc/`).

`basic/` and `misc/` are gitignored. Populate:

```bash
make -C thirdparty os-tests-sortix-clone
```

**Pruned on vendor** (sbunix has no pthread or network yet): `pthread`, `threads`,
`spawn`, `semaphore`, `sys_sem`, `arpa_inet`, `netinet_in`, `net_if`, `netdb`,
`sys_socket`. Re-run `os-tests-sortix-clone` after changing the prune list in
`thirdparty/Makefile` (`OSTEST_PRUNE_DIRS`).

### Build (host cross-compile → `thirdparty/os-tests-sortix/ostest/`)

```bash
# one test
make -C thirdparty os-tests-build OSTEST_TESTS="string/strlen"

# subdirectory
make -C thirdparty os-tests-build OSTEST_TESTS="string"

# all of basic/ (pthread/network dirs already pruned)
make -C thirdparty os-tests-build
```

Artifacts: `ostest/basic/` (ELFs), `ostest/report/` (`.out` / `.err`), `ostest/summary.txt`, `ostest/sources.list`.

Lists anything that did not link; details in `ostest/report/<test>.err`.

### Install (into initramfs staging)

```bash
make -C thirdparty os-tests-install
rm -f build/tarfs.o && make build/kernel.elf
make qemu
```

Copies **ok** ELFs to `build/rootfs/bin/os-tests-sortix/` → `/bin/os-tests-sortix/...` in the image.

Example: `/bin/os-tests-sortix/string/strlen`
